-- title:
--   U_q acts by a_q(g)∈{0,± 1} on λ-adic eigenvectors
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number and let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform, i.e. a normalised eigenform ($a_1(g)=1$, $a_{mn}(g)=a_m(g)a_n(g)$ for coprime $m,n$, and the recursions $a_{p^{r+2}}(g)=a_p(g)a_{p^{r+1}}(g)-p\,a_{p^r}(g)$ for $p\nmid M$ and $a_{p^{r+2}}(g)=a_p(g)a_{p^{r+1}}(g)$ for $p\mid M$) whose eigensystem occurs at no proper divisor $M'\mid M$, $M'\neq M$, in the sense that no normalised eigenform of weight two on $\Gamma_0(M')$ has the same $q$-coefficients at all primes not dividing $M$. Let $\lambda$ be a prime, $S$ a finite set of natural numbers, and $\chi_g$ a ring homomorphism to $\mathbb C$ from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(M)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S$ and $U_q$ for primes $q\mid M$, $q\notin S$ — such that $\chi_g(T_\ell)=a_\ell(g)$ for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$. Let $O''$ be a commutative $\mathbb Z_\lambda$-algebra, $K$ a field of characteristic zero which is an $O''$-algebra, and $\varphi$ a ring homomorphism from the image of $\chi_g$ into $K$; let $q$ be a prime dividing $M$ (no condition relating $q$ to $\lambda$ or to $S$). Give $J_0(M)=\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the modular function field of level $M$ over an algebraic closure of $\mathbb Q$ its [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleBar M`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeModule.html#L82) action of $\mathbb T=\mathbb Z[X_p : p \text{ prime}]$, and assume given: a $\mathbb Z_\lambda$-module structure on the Tate module $T_\lambda(J_0(M))$ (sequences $x$ in $J_0(M)$ with $x_0=0$ and $\lambda\, x_{n+1}=x_n$) for which $(a\cdot x)_n$ is the reduction of $a$ modulo $\lambda^n$ acting on $x_n$, and a ring homomorphism $TM$ from $\mathbb T$ to $\mathrm{End}_{O''}\bigl(O''\otimes_{\mathbb Z_\lambda}T_\lambda(J_0(M))\bigr)$ with $TM(t)(a\otimes x)=a\otimes(t\cdot x)$. Then there is an integer $a\in\{0,1,-1\}$ with $a_q(g)=a$ in $\mathbb C$ such that every vector $v$ of $K\otimes_{O''}\bigl(O''\otimes_{\mathbb Z_\lambda}T_\lambda(J_0(M))\bigr)$ satisfying $(TM(X_\ell))_K v=\varphi(\chi_g(T_\ell))\,v$ for all primes $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S$, also satisfies $(TM(X_q))_K v=a\,v$.
--
--   This is the Atkin–Lehner bound $a_q(g)\in\{0,\pm 1\}$ for a prime $q$ dividing the level of a weight-two newform, together with the statement that the corresponding generator of the Hecke algebra acts by this integer on the $\lambda$-adic Hecke eigenspace inside the Tate module of $J_0(M)$. It is the automorphic input to the local description at $q$ of the $\lambda$-adic representation attached to $g$, and is used in the construction of the ordinary line and of the torsion line at such primes.
